{"record_type":"timeline-node","type":"tool-after","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:41:40.830Z","data":{"input":{"tool":"read","sessionID":"ses_e8757c41fffeMKbFb1BEJd2CLi","callID":"call_720b5ffbff11419f88a3f34d26f7ad65","args":{"filePath":"README.md","offset":320,"limit":70}},"output":{"title":"README.md","output":"<path>README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n320: │       └── infrastructure/sqlite/\n321: │           └── sqlite-verification-repository.ts  # SQLite persistence\n322: │\n323: ├── test/                            # Tests\n324: ├── research/                        # Evaluation pipeline\n325: └── opencode-activity-captures/      # Runtime capture bundles\n326: ```\n327: \n328: ---\n329: \n330: ## Requirements\n331: \n332: - Node.js 22.22.2 or newer\n333: - npm 11 or newer\n334: - OpenCode for live capture\n335: - Ollama with a local extraction model (when model-based extraction enabled)\n336: \n337: ## Install\n338: \n339: ```powershell\n340: git clone <repository-url>\n341: cd traceforge\n342: npm install\n343: Copy-Item .env.example .env\n344: Copy-Item apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local\n345: npm run key:generate\n346: ```\n347: \n348: Put the generated encryption key in `.env`. Set the same `TRACEFORGE_API_TOKEN` in `.env` and `apps/web/.env.local`. Never commit either file.\n349: \n350: For local model extraction, install Ollama and configure:\n351: \n352: ```env\n353: TRACEFORGE_EXTRACTOR=ollama\n354: TRACEFORGE_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat\n355: TRACEFORGE_LLM_MODEL=qwen3.5:4b\n356: TRACEFORGE_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=180000\n357: ```\n358: \n359: Enable debug flow logs:\n360: ```env\n361: TRACEFORGE_DEBUG_FLOW=1\n362: ```\n363: \n364: ---\n365: \n366: ## Start TraceForge\n367: \n368: Run in separate terminals:\n369: \n370: ```powershell\n371: # Terminal 1: API Server (port 8080)\n372: npm run api:up\n373: \n374: # Terminal 2: Web Dashboard (port 3000)\n375: npm run web:dev\n376: ```\n377: \n378: Open `http://localhost:3000`. Check API health at `http://127.0.0.1:8080/healthz`.\n379: \n380: ---\n381: \n382: ## Blockchain Claim Anchoring (Sepolia and Sui Testnet)\n383: \n384: TraceForge can anchor a commitment for a **VERIFIED** claim on either Ethereum Sepolia or Sui Testnet. The dashboards provide separate **Anchor on Sepolia** and **Anchor on Sui** actions beside eligible claims. Each chain stores hashes and audit metadata; prompt text, source files, claim text, and evidence contents remain off-chain.\n385: \n386: ### What gets anchored\n387: \n388: The contract records a session/run hash, claim index, claim/audit manifest hash, evidence-root hash, schema version, chain timestamp, sender address, and a verified attestation. The raw prompt, source code, and evidence content are not sent to either chain. Each chain records its own transaction and event.\n389: \n\n(Showing lines 320-389 of 586. Use offset=390 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"│       └── infrastructure/sqlite/\n│           └── sqlite-verification-repository.ts  # SQLite persistence\n│\n├── test/                            # Tests\n├── research/                        # Evaluation pipeline\n└── opencode-activity-captures/      # Runtime capture bundles\n```\n\n---\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Node.js 22.22.2 or newer\n- npm 11 or newer\n- OpenCode for live capture\n- Ollama with a local extraction model (when model-based extraction enabled)\n\n## Install\n\n```powershell","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"README.md","text":"│       └── infrastructure/sqlite/\n│           └── sqlite-verification-repository.ts  # SQLite persistence\n│\n├── test/                            # Tests\n├── research/                        # Evaluation pipeline\n└── opencode-activity-captures/      # Runtime capture bundles\n```\n\n---\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Node.js 22.22.2 or newer\n- npm 11 or newer\n- OpenCode for live capture\n- Ollama with a local extraction model (when model-based extraction enabled)\n\n## Install\n\n```powershell\ngit clone <repository-url>\ncd traceforge\nnpm install\nCopy-Item .env.example .env\nCopy-Item apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local\nnpm run key:generate\n```\n\nPut the generated encryption key in `.env`. Set the same `TRACEFORGE_API_TOKEN` in `.env` and `apps/web/.env.local`. Never commit either file.\n\nFor local model extraction, install Ollama and configure:\n\n```env\nTRACEFORGE_EXTRACTOR=ollama\nTRACEFORGE_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat\nTRACEFORGE_LLM_MODEL=qwen3.5:4b\nTRACEFORGE_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=180000\n```\n\nEnable debug flow logs:\n```env\nTRACEFORGE_DEBUG_FLOW=1\n```\n\n---\n\n## Start TraceForge\n\nRun in separate terminals:\n\n```powershell\n# Terminal 1: API Server (port 8080)\nnpm run api:up\n\n# Terminal 2: Web Dashboard (port 3000)\nnpm run web:dev\n```\n\nOpen `http://localhost:3000`. Check API health at `http://127.0.0.1:8080/healthz`.\n\n---\n\n## Blockchain Claim Anchoring (Sepolia and Sui Testnet)\n\nTraceForge can anchor a commitment for a **VERIFIED** claim on either Ethereum Sepolia or Sui Testnet. The dashboards provide separate **Anchor on Sepolia** and **Anchor on Sui** actions beside eligible claims. Each chain stores hashes and audit metadata; prompt text, source files, claim text, and evidence contents remain off-chain.\n\n### What gets anchored\n\nThe contract records a session/run hash, claim index, claim/audit manifest hash, evidence-root hash, schema version, chain timestamp, sender address, and a verified attestation. The raw prompt, source code, and evidence content are not sent to either chain. Each chain records its own transaction and event.\n","lineStart":320,"lineEnd":389,"totalLines":586,"truncated":true}}}}}
