{"record_type":"timeline-node","type":"event","timestamp":"2026-10-28T12:42:32.427Z","data":{"event":{"id":"evt_182889869001Ck72nRdyctdTy3","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","part":{"id":"prt_1828882ef001Kqq3XjQP8VPlCy","messageID":"msg_182887aea0018n1383unEc8Cpw","sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","type":"reasoning","text":"Dist has stale compiled evaluate? It was modified in git status so dist maybe old. We'll need build. Need understand evidence references and dataset natural-v1 structure; prompts in dataset are synthetic? The instructions said inspect research dataset and annotation worksheet. Need create two separate annotation worksheets for human annotators. Existing annotations CSV is per-session with blank fields. We need create two worksheets that include session ID, prompt, final response, evidence references, hide predicted claims/verdicts. Should be CSV or maybe xlsx? We can create two separate CSVs (annotator A/B), one row per session or per potential claim? Annotators need fill claim rows. Existing annotations CSV has one row per session with blank claim fields. Better worksheets likely per session in CSV with columns session_id, prompt, final_response, evidence_references, annotation instructions and blank claim fields. Two separate files natural-v1.annotator-a.csv and natural-v1.annotator-b.csv, each with one row per session. But multiple claims per response need multiple rows. Could include \"annotator_rows\" with one row per session, claim_id blank, fields. Annotators can append rows. We can make it clearer: one row per session and prompts in CSV, plus columns for claims as repeated rows preallocated? Existing worksheet one row per session. The user asks \"two separate annotation worksheets for human annotators. Include session ID, prompt, final response, and evidence references. Hide TraceForge’s predicted claims and verdicts.\" We need preserve existing files. Create new files, don't overwrite annotations. Could create annotated worksheet CSV with 40 rows each, perhaps include claim_slot 1..? Hmm.\n\nNeed add conversion script reads completed, adjudicated annotations and creates natural-v1-adjudicated.jsonl. Preserve original evidence and validate every claim. It must not invent labels. Need handle completed annotations. Need decide input format. Likely use existing annotations CSV format (adjudicated_verdict) plus maybe two annotator sheets. \"Add a conversion script that reads the completed, adjudicated annotations and creates natural-v1-adjudicated.jsonl.\" Could be script reading natural-v1.annotations.csv (the adjudication sheet) and inject claims into dataset. Need validate every claim: exact quote occurs in final response, claim type valid, target etc, verdict valid, evidence IDs exist in that session's evidence, capture completeness. Also require adjudicated_verdict and maybe annotator A/B both non-empty, disagree? \"reads the completed, adjudicated annotations\" means only completed. Should reject if missing fields orunfinished. Need support claim rows. Existing worksheet has columns: session_id, claim_id, source_quote, claim_type, target, annotator_a_verdict, annotator_b_verdict, adjudicated_verdict, rationale, evidence_event_ids, capture_completeness. Need map to gold claim structure: claimIndex, claimText, claimType, target, expectedResult, sourceQuote? Let's inspect contracts/types to know ExtractedClaim fields and verdicts. Also export script and benchmark annotation.","time":{"start":1793191346927,"end":1793191352425}},"time":1793191352425}}}}
