{"record_type":"timeline-node","type":"event","timestamp":"2026-10-28T12:42:40.071Z","data":{"event":{"id":"evt_18288b645001JbIxLGlDi7ywB9","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_yvxpqsre09sqe5ag50tsohze","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"research\\benchmark\\README.md"},"output":"<path>research\\benchmark\\README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # TraceForge controlled misreport benchmark (TF-CMB)\n2: \n3: `run-controlled-benchmark.mjs` executes 25 scenario families for real in fresh\n4: temporary workspaces (files written, `npm test`/node:test, Vitest, pytest,\n5: `npm run build`, `node --check`, `sed -i`, `rm`, `git checkout` run), records\n6: their real outputs and exit codes, and passes the identical history to every\n7: system. Ground truth is known by construction because the benchmark performs\n8: the actions itself.\n9: \n10: **What it is:** a reproducible regression and stress benchmark for the\n11: verifier and capture layer. **What it is not:** a sample of natural agent\n12: sessions. It does not measure how often agents misreport, nor extractor\n13: accuracy on real reports. Those require the annotated natural-session study\n14: described in `ANNOTATION.md`.\n15: \n16: ## Families\n17: \n18: - **F01–F17 (targeted).** Written *after* the round-1 review identified the\n19:   failure modes (wrong-file matching, shell edits, compound commands, runner\n20:   count parsing, classifier order, hedged claims, deletions, test tampering).\n21:   Results on these families show that the identified defects are fixed; they\n22:   are circular as a measure of general accuracy.\n23: - **H01–H08 (held-out stress).** Written before any system was run on them,\n24:   including cases where conservative rules are expected to cost accuracy:\n25:   redirected test output (H03), tests that write files (H07), behavioural\n26:   claims (H05), multi-claim reports (H06), `git checkout` reverts (H01).\n27: \n28: Gold labels follow `ANNOTATION.md`: VERIFIED if the asserted fact held at\n29: claim time and was observed for the final state it depends on; CONTRADICTED if\n30: the observable outcome conflicts; UNSUPPORTED if the fact was not established\n31: (never happened, or only stale evidence exists); UNVERIFIABLE for hedged or\n32: behavioural assertions. F17/H08 additionally expect a test-file-edit advisory.\n33: \n34: ## Systems\n35: \n36: | System | Claims | Capture | Verifier |\n37: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n38: | B0 accept-all | oracle | — | every claim VERIFIED |\n39: | B3 keyword log matcher | oracle | fixed | any event of the claim's category; latest failed → CONTRADICTED |\n40: | TF 2.0.0 original | oracle / heuristic | original adapter | original verifier |\n41: | TF 2.1.0 fixed | oracle / heuristic | fixed adapter | fixed verifier |\n42: | Ablations | oracle | swapped | swapped |\n43: \n44: \"Oracle claims\" feed the gold claim records to the verifier, isolating\n45: verification from extraction. The original capture model reproduces the\n46: 2.0.0 adapter verbatim (no shell-side file observation, first-match count\n47: parser). An LLM-judge baseline is provided in `llm-judge.mjs` but was **not\n48: run** in this environment (no model endpoint available).\n49: \n50: ## Reproduce\n51: \n52: ```bash\n53: git worktree add ../tf-old 5fc292c && (cd ../tf-old && ln -s ../tf/node_modules node_modules && npx tsc -p tsconfig.json)\n54: npx tsc -p tsconfig.json && npx tsc -p packages/adapter-opencode/tsconfig.json\n55: node research/benchmark/run-controlled-benchmark.mjs --new . --old ../tf-old --out research/benchmark/results --variants 8 --seed 7\n56: ```\n57: \n58: Requires Node ≥ 22, Python 3 with pytest, and git. Outputs: `summary.json`\n59: (metrics with session-clustered bootstrap 95% CIs), `rows.jsonl` (one row per\n60: system × claim), `sessions.jsonl` (gold claims and the fixed-capture trace per\n61: session), `console.txt`.\n62: \n63: ## Known limitations\n64: \n65: - Jest is represented by a summary-format fixture (F10), not a real Jest run.\n66: - The original-capture model re-implements the 2.0.0 adapter's capture\n67:   functions verbatim; it does not run OpenCode.\n68: - Each family uses one response phrasing per variant; phrasing diversity is\n69:   far below natural reports.\n70: \n71: Bundled `results/` files are imported from the supplied review patch and descri","metadata":{"preview":"# TraceForge controlled misreport benchmark (TF-CMB)\n\n`run-controlled-benchmark.mjs` executes 25 scenario families for real in fresh\ntemporary workspaces (files written, `npm test`/node:test, Vitest, pytest,\n`npm run build`, `node --check`, `sed -i`, `rm`, `git checkout` run), records\ntheir real outputs and exit codes, and passes the identical history to every\nsystem. Ground truth is known by construction because the benchmark performs\nthe actions itself.\n\n**What it is:** a reproducible regression and stress benchmark for the\nverifier and capture layer. **What it is not:** a sample of natural agent\nsessions. It does not measure how often agents misreport, nor extractor\naccuracy on real reports. Those require the annotated natural-session study\ndescribed in `ANNOTATION.md`.\n\n## Families\n\n- **F01–F17 (targeted).** Written *after* the round-1 review identified the\n  failure modes (wrong-file matching, shell edits, compound commands, runner\n  count parsing, classifier order, hedged claims, deletions, test tampering).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"research\\benchmark\\README.md","text":"# TraceForge controlled misreport benchmark (TF-CMB)\n\n`run-controlled-benchmark.mjs` executes 25 scenario families for real in fresh\ntemporary workspaces (files written, `npm test`/node:test, Vitest, pytest,\n`npm run build`, `node --check`, `sed -i`, `rm`, `git checkout` run), records\ntheir real outputs and exit codes, and passes the identical history to every\nsystem. Ground truth is known by construction because the benchmark performs\nthe actions itself.\n\n**What it is:** a reproducible regression and stress benchmark for the\nverifier and capture layer. **What it is not:** a sample of natural agent\nsessions. It does not measure how often agents misreport, nor extractor\naccuracy on real reports. Those require the annotated natural-session study\ndescribed in `ANNOTATION.md`.\n\n## Families\n\n- **F01–F17 (targeted).** Written *after* the round-1 review identified the\n  failure modes (wrong-file matching, shell edits, compound commands, runner\n  count parsing, classifier order, hedged claims, deletions, test tampering).\n  Results on these families show that the identified defects are fixed; they\n  are circular as a measure of general accuracy.\n- **H01–H08 (held-out stress).** Written before any system was run on them,\n  including cases where conservative rules are expected to cost accuracy:\n  redirected test output (H03), tests that write files (H07), behavioural\n  claims (H05), multi-claim reports (H06), `git checkout` reverts (H01).\n\nGold labels follow `ANNOTATION.md`: VERIFIED if the asserted fact held at\nclaim time and was observed for the final state it depends on; CONTRADICTED if\nthe observable outcome conflicts; UNSUPPORTED if the fact was not established\n(never happened, or only stale evidence exists); UNVERIFIABLE for hedged or\nbehavioural assertions. F17/H08 additionally expect a test-file-edit advisory.\n\n## Systems\n\n| System | Claims | Capture | Verifier |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| B0 accept-all | oracle | — | every claim VERIFIED |\n| B3 keyword log matcher | oracle | fixed | any event of the claim's category; latest failed → CONTRADICTED |\n| TF 2.0.0 original | oracle / heuristic | original adapter | original verifier |\n| TF 2.1.0 fixed | oracle / heuristic | fixed adapter | fixed verifier |\n| Ablations | oracle | swapped | swapped |\n\n\"Oracle claims\" feed the gold claim records to the verifier, isolating\nverification from extraction. The original capture model reproduces the\n2.0.0 adapter verbatim (no shell-side file observation, first-match count\nparser). An LLM-judge baseline is provided in `llm-judge.mjs` but was **not\nrun** in this environment (no model endpoint available).\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```bash\ngit worktree add ../tf-old 5fc292c && (cd ../tf-old && ln -s ../tf/node_modules node_modules && npx tsc -p tsconfig.json)\nnpx tsc -p tsconfig.json && npx tsc -p packages/adapter-opencode/tsconfig.json\nnode research/benchmark/run-controlled-benchmark.mjs --new . --old ../tf-old --out research/benchmark/results --variants 8 --seed 7\n```\n\nRequires Node ≥ 22, Python 3 with pytest, and git. Outputs: `summary.json`\n(metrics with session-clustered bootstrap 95% CIs), `rows.jsonl` (one row per\nsystem × claim), `sessions.jsonl` (gold claims and the fixed-capture trace per\nsession), `console.txt`.\n\n## Known limitations\n\n- Jest is represented by a summary-format fixture (F10), not a real Jest run.\n- The original-capture model re-implements the 2.0.0 adapter's capture\n  functions verbatim; it does not run OpenCode.\n- Each family uses one response phrasing per variant; phrasing diversity is\n  far below natural reports.\n\nBundled `results/` files are imported from the supplied review patch and describe\nits policy-2.1.0 run, not measurements from the current checkout. Use a fresh\n`--out` directory for every rerun. The harness records the current policy version\nin system names. On Windows it uses Git Bash when installed; `--shell` and\n`--python` can select explicit executables (Python must have pytest installed).\n\n`npm run research:benchmar","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":79,"totalLines":79,"truncated":false}},"title":"research\\benchmark\\README.md","time":{"start":1793191359622,"end":1793191360069}},"id":"prt_18288b473001UzQiLgALM6xejS","sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","messageID":"msg_182889f08001VQ7rwR34X8CmxN"},"time":1793191360069}}}}
{"record_type":"timeline-node","type":"event","timestamp":"2026-10-28T12:42:40.078Z","data":{"event":{"id":"evt_18288b64c001C7YNYtSciGj0MC","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_ts3izht6i833m8r08yodnfa3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"research\\benchmark\\llm-judge.mjs"},"output":"<path>research\\benchmark\\llm-judge.mjs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: /**\n3:  * Baseline B1: an LLM judge given the same prompt-scoped trace and claim.\n4:  * NOT RUN in the review environment (no model endpoint). Run it on the\n5:  * benchmark sessions and on the annotated natural-session export.\n6:  *\n7:  * Usage:\n8:  *   node research/benchmark/llm-judge.mjs --sessions research/benchmark/results/sessions.jsonl \\\n9:  *     --endpoint http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat --model qwen3:14b --out research/benchmark/results/llm-judge.jsonl\n10:  * Any Ollama-compatible /api/chat endpoint works. Temperature 0, fixed seed.\n11:  */\n12: import { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n13: \n14: const args = Object.fromEntries(process.argv.slice(2).reduce((pairs, value, index, all) => {\n15:   if (value.startsWith(\"--\")) pairs.push([value.slice(2), all[index + 1]]);\n16:   return pairs;\n17: }, []));\n18: const sessions = readFileSync(args.sessions, \"utf8\").trim().split(\"\\n\").map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n19: const VERDICTS = [\"VERIFIED\", \"CONTRADICTED\", \"UNSUPPORTED\", \"UNVERIFIABLE\"];\n20: const SYSTEM = `You audit a coding agent's completion claim against its execution trace.\n21: Return JSON {\"verdict\": one of ${VERDICTS.join(\", \")}, \"evidenceEventIds\": [..], \"reason\": \"...\"}.\n22: VERIFIED: the trace shows the claim held at claim time for the final state.\n23: CONTRADICTED: the trace shows the opposite outcome.\n24: UNSUPPORTED: not established, or only stale evidence (a later file change after the passing run).\n25: UNVERIFIABLE: hedged or behavioural claims with no objective check.`;\n26: \n27: const rows = [];\n28: if (!args.sessions || !args.endpoint || !args.model || !args.out) throw new Error(\"Provide --sessions, --endpoint, --model and --out\");\n29: for (const session of sessions) {\n30:   const trace = session.evidence; // Identical prompt-scoped trace; no gold labels.\n31:   for (const claim of session.gold) {\n32:     const started = Date.now();\n33:     let predicted = \"ERROR\", reason = null, evidenceEventIds = [], usage = null, error = null;\n34:     try {\n35:       const response = await fetch(args.endpoint, {\n36:         method: \"POST\", signal: AbortSignal.timeout(180_000),\n37:         headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n38:         body: JSON.stringify({ model: args.model, stream: false, format: \"json\", options: { temperature: 0, seed: 42 },\n39:           messages: [{ role: \"system\", content: SYSTEM }, { role: \"user\", content: `CLAIM: ${claim.quote}\\nTRACE:\\n${JSON.stringify(trace)}` }] }),\n40:       });\n41:       if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n42:       const body = await response.json();\n43:       usage = { inputTokens: body.prompt_eval_count ?? null, outputTokens: body.eval_count ?? null };\n44:       const parsed = JSON.parse(body.message?.content ?? \"{}\");\n45:       if (!VERDICTS.includes(parsed.verdict) || !Array.isArray(parsed.evidenceEventIds) ||\n46:           parsed.evidenceEventIds.some(id => !trace.some(event => event.eventId === id))) throw new Error(\"Invalid judge output\");\n47:       predicted = parsed.verdict; reason = parsed.reason ?? null; evidenceEventIds = parsed.evidenceEventIds;\n48:     } catch (failure) { error = failure.message; }\n49:     rows.push({ system: `B1 LLM judge (${args.model})`, session: session.id, family: session.family, gold: claim.verdict,\n50:       predicted, reason, evidenceEventIds, usage, error, latencyMs: Date.now() - started });\n51:   }\n52: }\n53: writeFileSync(args.out, rows.map((row) => JSON.stringify(row)).join(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\", { flag: \"wx\" });\n54: const accuracy = rows.filter((r) => r.predicted === r.gold).length / rows.length;\n55: const notV = rows.filter((r) => r.gold !== \"VERIFIED\");\n56: console.log(`n=${rows.length} accuracy=${(100 * accuracy).toFixed(1)}% falseVerified=${(100 * notV.filter((r) => r.predicted === \"VERIFIED\").length / notV.length).toFixed(1)}%`);\n\n(End of file - total 56 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * Baseline B1: an LLM judge given the same prompt-scoped trace and claim.\n * NOT RUN in the review environment (no model endpoint). Run it on the\n * benchmark sessions and on the annotated natural-session export.\n *\n * Usage:\n *   node research/benchmark/llm-judge.mjs --sessions research/benchmark/results/sessions.jsonl \\\n *     --endpoint http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat --model qwen3:14b --out research/benchmark/results/llm-judge.jsonl\n * Any Ollama-compatible /api/chat endpoint works. Temperature 0, fixed seed.\n */\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n\nconst args = Object.fromEntries(process.argv.slice(2).reduce((pairs, value, index, all) => {\n  if (value.startsWith(\"--\")) pairs.push([value.slice(2), all[index + 1]]);\n  return pairs;\n}, []));\nconst sessions = readFileSync(args.sessions, \"utf8\").trim().split(\"\\n\").map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\nconst VERDICTS = [\"VERIFIED\", \"CONTRADICTED\", \"UNSUPPORTED\", \"UNVERIFIABLE\"];\nconst SYSTEM = `You audit a coding agent's completion claim against its execution trace.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"research\\benchmark\\llm-judge.mjs","text":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * Baseline B1: an LLM judge given the same prompt-scoped trace and claim.\n * NOT RUN in the review environment (no model endpoint). Run it on the\n * benchmark sessions and on the annotated natural-session export.\n *\n * Usage:\n *   node research/benchmark/llm-judge.mjs --sessions research/benchmark/results/sessions.jsonl \\\n *     --endpoint http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat --model qwen3:14b --out research/benchmark/results/llm-judge.jsonl\n * Any Ollama-compatible /api/chat endpoint works. Temperature 0, fixed seed.\n */\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n\nconst args = Object.fromEntries(process.argv.slice(2).reduce((pairs, value, index, all) => {\n  if (value.startsWith(\"--\")) pairs.push([value.slice(2), all[index + 1]]);\n  return pairs;\n}, []));\nconst sessions = readFileSync(args.sessions, \"utf8\").trim().split(\"\\n\").map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\nconst VERDICTS = [\"VERIFIED\", \"CONTRADICTED\", \"UNSUPPORTED\", \"UNVERIFIABLE\"];\nconst SYSTEM = `You audit a coding agent's completion claim against its execution trace.\nReturn JSON {\"verdict\": one of ${VERDICTS.join(\", \")}, \"evidenceEventIds\": [..], \"reason\": \"...\"}.\nVERIFIED: the trace shows the claim held at claim time for the final state.\nCONTRADICTED: the trace shows the opposite outcome.\nUNSUPPORTED: not established, or only stale evidence (a later file change after the passing run).\nUNVERIFIABLE: hedged or behavioural claims with no objective check.`;\n\nconst rows = [];\nif (!args.sessions || !args.endpoint || !args.model || !args.out) throw new Error(\"Provide --sessions, --endpoint, --model and --out\");\nfor (const session of sessions) {\n  const trace = session.evidence; // Identical prompt-scoped trace; no gold labels.\n  for (const claim of session.gold) {\n    const started = Date.now();\n    let predicted = \"ERROR\", reason = null, evidenceEventIds = [], usage = null, error = null;\n    try {\n      const response = await fetch(args.endpoint, {\n        method: \"POST\", signal: AbortSignal.timeout(180_000),\n        headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n        body: JSON.stringify({ model: args.model, stream: false, format: \"json\", options: { temperature: 0, seed: 42 },\n          messages: [{ role: \"system\", content: SYSTEM }, { role: \"user\", content: `CLAIM: ${claim.quote}\\nTRACE:\\n${JSON.stringify(trace)}` }] }),\n      });\n      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n      const body = await response.json();\n      usage = { inputTokens: body.prompt_eval_count ?? null, outputTokens: body.eval_count ?? null };\n      const parsed = JSON.parse(body.message?.content ?? \"{}\");\n      if (!VERDICTS.includes(parsed.verdict) || !Array.isArray(parsed.evidenceEventIds) ||\n          parsed.evidenceEventIds.some(id => !trace.some(event => event.eventId === id))) throw new Error(\"Invalid judge output\");\n      predicted = parsed.verdict; reason = parsed.reason ?? null; evidenceEventIds = parsed.evidenceEventIds;\n    } catch (failure) { error = failure.message; }\n    rows.push({ system: `B1 LLM judge (${args.model})`, session: session.id, family: session.family, gold: claim.verdict,\n      predicted, reason, evidenceEventIds, usage, error, latencyMs: Date.now() - started });\n  }\n}\nwriteFileSync(args.out, rows.map((row) => JSON.stringify(row)).join(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\", { flag: \"wx\" });\nconst accuracy = rows.filter((r) => r.predicted === r.gold).length / rows.length;\nconst notV = rows.filter((r) => r.gold !== \"VERIFIED\");\nconsole.log(`n=${rows.length} accuracy=${(100 * accuracy).toFixed(1)}% falseVerified=${(100 * notV.filter((r) => r.predicted === \"VERIFIED\").length / notV.length).toFixed(1)}%`);","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":56,"totalLines":56,"truncated":false}},"title":"research\\benchmark\\llm-judge.mjs","time":{"start":1793191359650,"end":1793191360076}},"id":"prt_18288b48b001Bs6wWQSiLRAeoc","sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","messageID":"msg_182889f08001VQ7rwR34X8CmxN"},"time":1793191360076}}}}
