{"record_type":"timeline-node","type":"event","timestamp":"2026-10-28T12:44:57.839Z","data":{"event":{"id":"evt_1828ad06d001x1cWYA2mHgj9zy","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","part":{"id":"prt_1828aa88c001OrpMUVXN6XG4n0","messageID":"msg_1828a9de3001VZQsju1VIzM1nk","sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","type":"reasoning","text":"Predicted max claims 13. But human gold may differ. Preallocate 15? 40*15*2 = 1200 rows, evidence repeated. 221KB*15=3.3MB each + duplicated final/prompt. ~4MB each. Fine. But unwieldy. Maybe preallocate 5 for most? We can generate one row per session with 15 claim slot columns? No.\n\nAlternative: worksheets as two JSONL files, one object per session containing `claims` array blank. But not spreadsheet. Could provide both CSV and JSON? \"two separate annotation worksheets\" maybe two files, could be JSONL. But \"worksheet\" usually CSV. Let's do CSV with one row per session and an embedded claims template as JSON? Hmm.\n\nI think 6 slots is enough and instruct to add rows. But session with 13 claims would need extra. Since predicted claims are hidden, instruct that if >6, insert additional rows copying context. That's okay. Use 6 slots. Maybe 8 to be safe. 8*40=320 rows. We'll do 8.\n\nNeed hide predictions: ensure no `traceforge_verdict`, no `gold_verdict`, no `claim_text` from claims.csv, no goldClaims. Evidence references might include `metadata` but not predictions. Ensure script explicitly whitelists dataset fields and evidence fields. It must not read claims.csv. Good.\n\nNeed conversion script input. We can design a new adjudication CSV header with columns:\n`session_id,claim_id,source_quote,claim_type,target,expected_result,annotator_a_verdict,annotator_b_verdict,adjudicated_verdict,rationale,evidence_event_ids,test_tampering,capture_completeness,adjudication_status`\nExisting annotations file lacks expected_result, test_tampering, adjudication_status. To preserve existing, conversion can accept legacy header too by treating missing columns as blank and requiring adjudication_status optional? But rigorous \"do not mark unfinished annotations as adjudicated\" means we should require explicit status. Yet existing annotations file is the worksheet provided. Maybe we should create `natural-v1.adjudications.csv` template with the new header. Conversion requires `adjudication_status=ADJUDICATED`. It can also read legacy `natural-v1.annotations.csv` if all rows complete? Hmm. If no status column, can't prove adjudication. Better not support legacy? But the user says \"reads the completed, adjudicated annotations\" perhaps they expect existing annotations file. Wecan update existing? No, preserve existing files. We can leave existing and add `natural-v1.adjudications.csv` template. Conversion reads that. But then two annotator worksheets plus adjudication template. Good.\n\nCould add `research/annotation/README.md` with instructions and exact fill fields.\n\nNeed perhaps generate adjudication template from blank. But user only asked two worksheets. Conversion script can accept two raw annotator worksheets and create adjudication? No. Let's include an adjudication template as a tool. It can be empty per session? We could derive from annotator sheets after both completed:\n- `merge-annotations.mjs --a ... --b ... --out natural-v1.adjudications.csv`\nThis creates rows keyed by claim_id, aligns exact source quotes; leaves adjudicated verdict blank where disagree and requires human fill. But user didn't ask. Yet it supports workflow. Might be overkill but useful and helps convert. However \"Add a conversion script\" singular. Too many scripts might be okay.\n\nFocus:\n1. `research/annotation/prepare-worksheets.mjs` generates two CSVs (and maybe adjudication template) from dataset.\n2. `research/annotation/build-adjudicated-dataset.mjs` converts adjudicated CSV to JSONL with validation.\n3. `research/annotation/run-evaluation-suite.mjs` runs direct node evaluation commands into fresh dirs after labels exist. It must also validate that annotations exist, and refuse if no adjudicated file. But it can't create labels.\n4. `research/annotation/README.md` instructions.\n5. Tests? Add `test/research-annotation-tools.test.ts` or .mjs test run via vitest. But our scripts are .mjs; can test with child_process. Need ensure typecheck. Could add unit tests importing? .mjs no ","time":{"start":1793191487628,"end":1793191497837}},"time":1793191497837}}}}
