{"record_type":"timeline-node","type":"event","timestamp":"2026-10-28T12:47:01.030Z","data":{"event":{"id":"evt_1828cb1a1001Wi2xoM9ULVJVdV","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","part":{"id":"prt_1828be8d4001crH6RhUMAbU2vZ","messageID":"msg_1828bded0001mjEO2TKJQa3ePo","sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","type":"reasoning","text":"research/runs not ignored. Should we add to .gitignore? User said save outputs in fresh dir. Adding `research/runs/` to gitignore might be okay but modifies existing .gitignore. Not necessary; we won't run actual evals. But wrapper when run later will create outputs untracked. Could add .gitignore line? Maybe not to avoid unasked changes. Could use `.traceforge/research-runs` ignored. But user says fresh output directory. Use `research/runs` and no run now. Fine.\n\nNeed maybe include `research/datasets` currently untracked; our new files there. Fine.\n\nLet's design exact scripts.\n\n### prepare-worksheets.mjs\n\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport fs...\nconst args = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\nconst dataset = resolve(args.dataset ?? \"research/datasets/natural-v1.jsonl\");\nconst outDir = resolve(args.outDir ?? dirname(dataset));\nconst slots = Number(args.slots ?? 10);\nconst rows = read JSONL\nvalidate unique ids, finalResponse string, evidence array\nconst evidenceRefs = evidence.map(e => ({\n eventId, sequenceNumber, eventType, outcome, occurredAt, ...(target?{target}:{}),\n metadata: e.metadata\n}))\nfor annotator A/B:\n  columns [...]\n  for session:\n    for slot 1..slots:\n      row fields...\n  write `natural-v1.annotator-${a}.csv` with `flag: wx`? If file exists, fail to avoid overwrite. But if we rerun after changes, need --force. User said preserve existing. Add --force only explicit. We'll generate once.\n```\n\nMaybe one row per session only with `claim_slot` 1..10 is okay. But repeated evidence maybe huge. Let's use a normalized approach: `natural-v1.annotator-a.csv` with one row per claim slot; evidence refs repeated. Let's check output size after. Fine.\n\nName header fields perhaps `prompt` not `promptQuery`, `final_response`, `evidence_references`. Include `session_id`. Good.\n\n`worksheet_id`: `${session.id}:${slot}`. `annotator_id`: \"annotator-a\"/\"annotator-b\". Maybe hidden no TraceForge data.\n\n`annotation_status`: allowed `COMPLETE`, `NO_CLAIMS`, `INCOMPLETE`. Prefilled blank. For no-claims session, they fill one row's status `NO_CLAIMS` and leave other slots maybe blank. But conversion reads adjudication, not worksheets. We can define worksheet instructions.\n\nMaybe worksheets need `claim_id` blank. They fill C1 etc.\n\nAdd `source_quote` exact, `claim_type`, `target`, `expected_result`, `verdict`, rationale, evidence_event_ids, test_tampering, capture_completeness, annotation_status, notes. `evidence_event_ids` as JSON array or semicolon separated; instruct.\n\nShould annotator worksheet include `annotator_verdict` rather than `verdict`? Call `annotator_verdict`. Good.\n\n### Conversion script\n\nNeed CSV parser. Implement robust RFC4180 parse.\n\nHeader sets:\nRequired:\n- session_id\n- claim_id\n- source_quote\n- claim_type\n- target\n- expected_result (optional derive)\n- annotator_a_verdict\n- annotator_b_verdict\n- adjudicated_verdict\n- rationale\n- evidence_event_ids\n- test_tampering\n- capture_completeness\n- adjudication_status\n- adjudicator_id\n- adjudicated_at\n\nMaybe `claim_id` blank for NO_CLAIMS marker. `session_status` instead of inferring. Add `session_status` required with `CLAIMS_PRESENT` or `NO_CLAIMS`. For claim rows, `CLAIMS_PRESENT`.\n- For NO_CLAIMS row: claim_id/source_quote/claim_type/target/expected_result/verdicts/rationale/evidence_event_ids/test_tampering blank? maybe capture completeness, adjudication_status, adjudicator, date, session_status. Require annotator_a_verdict/annotator_b? To prove both annotators agree no claims, use `annotator_a_verdict` = \"NO_CLAIMS\", `annotator_b_verdict` = \"NO_CLAIMS\", adjudicated_verdict = \"NO_CLAIMS\". This is a status, but field is verdict. Could allow those special values only on no-claims rows. Rationale nonempty (\"both annotators found no claims\"). Evidence_event_ids [] or blank. test_tampering FALSE. This gives adjudication. Good. But verdicts fields normally only valid verdicts. Special-case.\n- For claim rows: require both verdicts valid, adjudicated valid. If A==B and adjudicated equal, f","time":{"start":1793191569620,"end":1793191621024}},"time":1793191621025}}}}
