d blank columns. But then claim rows? Could preallocate 10 slots per session → similar size. Maybe generated from `prepare-worksheets` as extra file. Not required. Hmm.\n\nWe should consider adding a merge script to reduce manual effort and enforce A/B raw labels. Could add, but task didn't ask and time. Maybe tests enough.\n\nNeed test runner dry run maybe no test. Fine.\n\nNeed check README path references and instructions no issue.\n\nNeed perhaps add `research/runs/` to .gitignore? Not necessary; no actual run. But if user later runs, output would be untracked. Maybe okay. Could mention. Don't modify.\n\nNeed ensure worksheets include \"evidence references\" not full evidence. We included metadata full. Good. Verify they don't include predictions hidden in metadata? The dataset evidence metadata might contain study or claims? Let's search for \"verdict\" or \"claim\" in worksheet. It's possible prompt text contains \"claim\"? But predicted claims/verdicts? Let's search literal `\"verdict\"` and `TraceForge` etc. We checked no `traceforge_verdict`, `gold_verdict`. Could include \"verdict\" in text? The prompt maybe \"verdict\"? Let's check.","time":{"start":1793191859752,"end":1793191865880}},"time":1793191865880}}}}
