 focus on controlled-v1 conversion and experiments. Need maybe first estimate runtime. Create controlled dataset and run fast deterministic/heuristic/accept/regex. Then run Ollama extraction on maybe all 200. Then judges. We'll see.\n\nNeed write converter script. Could place in `research/annotation/build-controlled-dataset.mjs`. It reads `research/benchmark/results/sessions.jsonl` (or arg `--sessions`) and writes `research/datasets/controlled-v1.jsonl` plus CSV exports maybe later. We need ensure preserve bundled results (read-only). Use `flag wx` to avoid overwrite. We can just convert; no need to modify benchmark.\n\nMapping:\n- expected result map same as conversion.\n- target: gold.target. Some targets \"test execution\", \"build\", \"task\". Fine.\n- claim text quote exact. `sourceQuote`.\n- `verdict` from gold.\n- `testTampering`: gold.advisory bool.\n- `family`: metadata.\n- `promptQuery`: maybe `Controlled benchmark scenario family ${family}.` Need target? Could use `''`? Judge system gets promptQuery; empty okay. Better provide a meaningful generic prompt: `Controlled benchmark scenario: ${family}. Judge only the supplied claim against the trace.` But that might bias judge? It's consistent across all. The benchmark response is a completion report; the original task is implicit. We can set `promptQuery` to `Controlled benchmark family: ${family}`. Fine.\n- `metadata`: `{ source: \"research/benchmark/results/sessions.jsonl\", family, variant: id split #, labelProvenance: \"controlled benchmark actions; known by construction; not human-adjudicated\", finalDigest, collectionMetadata: { taskId: family } }`.\n- `annotationStatus: \"controlled\"`.\n- `evidence`: keep exact array. Ensure promptId all same? yes \"p\".\n- Validate unique ids, quotes exact, claim types, verdicts, evidence.\n\nAlso export `controlled-v1.sessions.csv` and `.claims.csv`? We can have converter write CSV alongside with >5x rows:\n  - sessions.csv 200 rows: session_id,family,response,prompt,evidence_count,gold_claim_count,label_provenance\n  - gold-claims.csv 216 rows: session_id,family,claim_index,source_quote,claim_type,target,expected_result,verdict,test_tampering,capture_completeness\n  - evidence.csv maybe all events (how many? 200 * ~4 = 800+) with session_id,event_id,seq,type,outcome,target,metadata. More than 5x. Useful for reviewers.\nWrite to `research/exports/controlled-v1/`? User wants all CSV files. May","time":{"start":1793192382106,"end":1793192395028}},"time":1793192395028}}}}
