{"record_type":"timeline-node","type":"event","timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:01:27.497Z","data":{"event":{"id":"evt_18299ea460019gTTu03IPSyMQq","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","part":{"id":"prt_18299cbf1001Ro5W3VQvTPSCKx","messageID":"msg_18299bf69001rUF5ghWqErcGCG","sessionID":"ses_e7d7ba936ffeOnBhTlKsfisQhw","type":"reasoning","text":"Rows 1728 = 8 systems * 216 claims. Great. 5x. We can export all to CSV. Existing benchmark results are legit controlled. New evaluations add 4 systems? Actually evaluate with oracle/heuristic × three baselines = 6 systems; ollama deterministic = 1; llm judge =1; agent judge=1. Total 9 new.\n\nNeed maybe run controlled benchmark harness to produce fresh 200 sessions? Existing sessions are from bundled results and timestamps 2026-10-28, same current. They are legitimate controlled benchmark sessions. We can use.\n\nNeed perhaps adapt evaluate to use controlled labels without \"annotated\" false label. We'll add `--allow-unadjudicated` to runner. Let's modify runner. Also maybe add `--status controlled`? Keep allow flag. The manifest will show `allowUnadjudicated: true`. Good.\n\nLet's write controlled converter script. Also export benchmark CSVs in same script or separate. Perhaps converter writes:\n- dataset JSONL\n- sessions.csv\n- gold-claims.csv\n- evidence.csv\n- benchmark-summary.csv (from summary.json)\n- benchmark-rows.csv (from rows.jsonl)\n- benchmark-heldout-summary.csv maybe.\nThis produces all CSV files >5x. We can also later export new evaluation results.\n\nLet's inspect `summary.json` heldOut etc for CSV. We can flatten arrays. Write in script.\n\nNeed maybe `rows.jsonl` has all 1728 rows; export to CSV. Good.\n\nNeed maybe \"more than 5x data\" = 200 sessions and 216 claims; evidence 536. The rows file 1728. Good.\n\nLet's implement `research/annotation/build-controlled-dataset.mjs`. It should read `research/benchmark/results/sessions.jsonl` and summary/rows. Output `research/datasets/controlled-v1.jsonl` and `research/exports/controlled-v1/*.csv`. Use `flag wx` unless `--force`. Validate.\n\nNeed promptQuery maybe family humanized. Could map family to sentence. Maybe use:\n`Controlled benchmark scenario ${family}. The agent's final response is evaluated against a trace produced by executing the scenario.` This is a generic prompt, but judge sees it. It doesn't leak gold. Fine.\nMaybe use empty prompt to avoid bias? The judge system expects prompt query; evidence contains final response. For controlled benchmark, the \"prompt\" is not the original task. A generic prompt might bias but same for all. We can set `promptQuery: \"\"` and note unavailable. The benchmark harness's llm-judge uses only claim and trace, not prompt. The evaluate modelJudge uses promptQuery and finalResponse; empty is okay. For comparability, maybe set `promptQuery` to `\"\"`. But reviewers might want prompt. We can set `promptQuery: \"Controlled benchmark scenario: \" + family` and metadata `promptUnavailable: true`. Does that constitute invented prompt? It's not human prompt; we should not pretend. Better set promptQuery to `\"\"` and metadata `promptAvailable:false`. The judge still has claim + final response + evidence. Good. But evaluate's metric doesn't use prompt except judge. The agent judge may benefit from response. Fine.\n\nNeed expectedResult mapping. For TEST_PASSED, standard \"exitCode equals 0 and failed equals 0\"; gold may have target \"test execution\". For FILE_CREATED standard. Good.\nNeed maybe claimText should be quote. Source quote exact. Validate.\nNeed claimIndex sequential. Gold order.\nNeed annotationStatus \"controlled\". The evaluate runner will allow with flag.\nNeed maybe `metadata.collectionMetadata.taskId` = family for task clustering. Runner uses session cluster. Fine.\nNeed `metadata.family`, `variant`, `labelProvenance`, `sourceFile`, `finalDigest`.\nNeed evidence copied exactly. `promptId` p.\nNeed maybe `evidence` events have `promptId: \"p\"` all same.\n\nWrite CSV with columns. Use `toCsv` from lib. For evidence metadata JSON. Sessions CSV includes promptQuery empty, response, family, counts, digest. Gold claims CSV includes test_tampering from advisory and capture completeness \"COMPLETE\" (controlled). Is that inventing? Capture completeness for controlled benchmark is complete by construction; okay, but it's not human annotation. Mark label_provenance. Coul","time":{"start":1793192479729,"end":1793192487494}},"time":1793192487494}}}}
